cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'LoRaCAP: a field-calibrated LoRaWAN uplink capacity simulator'
message: >-
  If LoRaCAP contributes to published work, please cite it. If you use it
  for a specific deployment study, cite the paper reporting that study as
  well.
type: software
# NOTE for double-blind review: this file identifies the authors. Remove or
# redact it from any reviewer-facing copy, and prefer an anonymised mirror
# (for example anonymous.4open.science) or a restricted-access deposit with a
# reviewer token over a public repository.
authors:
  - given-names: Wilder
    family-names: Castellanos
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0311-492X'
    affiliation: 'School of Engineering, Pontificia Universidad Javeriana, Bogotá, Colombia'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/wilcashe/loracap'
abstract: >-
  LoRaCAP is a LoRaWAN uplink capacity simulator in which the engine is
  independent of any particular deployment. A site is described in a single
  study file and the rest is automatic. The collision model re-implements LoRaSim (Bor et al.,
  MSWiM 2016) in Python 3 and extends it with direct multi-channel simulation
  instead of single-channel extrapolation, an enforced chip-wide
  simultaneous-demodulation limit, and node placement over a real site
  boundary rather than a theoretical coverage disc. Reports the Data
  Extraction Rate against node count with mean and standard deviation over
  repeated runs, and derives the capacity at a chosen threshold with a
  bootstrap confidence interval. Includes tools to convert a KML boundary and
  to fit a log-distance propagation model from field measurements.
keywords:
  - LoRaWAN
  - LPWAN
  - network scalability
  - discrete-event simulation
  - path loss
  - Internet of Things
license: MIT
license-url: 'https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT'
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-10-20'
references:
  - type: article
    title: 'Do LoRa Low-Power Wide-Area Networks Scale?'
    authors:
      - given-names: Martin
        family-names: Bor
      - given-names: Utz
        family-names: Roedig
      - given-names: Thiemo
        family-names: Voigt
      - given-names: Juan
        family-names: Alonso
    year: 2016
    doi: 10.1145/2988287.2989163
    notes: >-
      Source of the collision model re-implemented in loracap/core.py.
      LoRaSim 0.2.1 is licensed CC BY 4.0.
